CONCEPT: Because the speed of light is the same for every observer, the same two events (pulse emitted, pulse received) trace a short straight path in the shuttle frame but a longer diagonal path for an Earth observer, so the Earth observer must record a longer elapsed time — time dilation.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): If light must travel at c for both observers, then a longer light path can only mean a longer elapsed time — the Earth observer's diagonal hypotenuse is literally the extra time the moving clock 'loses'.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

